---
source: crates/cli/tests/init.rs
expression: "format!(\"{yaml}---\\n{}\", text(&out.stdout))"
---
# Generated by `sudsy init --from csharpier`; review before use.
extends:
  - preset:csharp/csharpier-compat
csharp:
  format:
    end_of_line: lf
    indent_size: 4
    indent_style: tab
    line_width: 120
---
migrated .csharpierrc.yaml
extends: preset:csharp/csharpier-compat
not migrated: overrides (`overrides` applies options per glob; there is no `formatter` key to treat other extensions (.csr, .cst) as C#; a `.csx` with `#r` or `#load` fails to parse (the worker parses scripts as ordinary files))
not migrated: preprocessorSymbolSets (The configured sets are not read (the value format is undocumented): csharp/csharpier-compat derives the sets from the conditions of each file instead; a branch no subset of those symbols activates (`#if false`) stays verbatim)

Add to .editorconfig (or run again with --write-editorconfig):

# Added by `sudsy init`: Sudsy formats and lints these.
[*.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.IDE0055.severity = none

note: set EnforceCodeStyleInBuild to true (Directory.Build.props) so the SDK reports the other IDE* style rules during `dotnet build`
